# flow -- the mutants of src/ztypecheck/flow.z that no test can kill, each with the reason:
# `zgate mutate` (make mutate) leaves them out of the score and lists them apart in
# survivors.md. A row names a mutant by the function its edit is in, the kind of the edit
# (op, as mutsites names it) and which of the function's edits of that kind it is, from 1,
# so an edit elsewhere in the file does not move it. A row whose function or count changes
# names another mutant: check the rows of a function after editing it.

# equivalent -- one mutant no program can tell from zc: where, which edit, and why
equivalent: data {
    where: text
    op: text
    nth: u64
    why: text
}

